Theorem TF-1: Side-table domain types — borrow_sources, project_alias_sources, Return Provenance

  Preconditions:
    - Auxiliary side tables carry per-variable provenance the lattice
      cannot express per Annex E §AIMS.9
    - Side tables are NOT lattice dimensions; they are typed pre-pass
      or intra-pass annotations consumed by specific DP / TF / RL rules
    - borrow_sources populated by TF-4 (Project) per Annex E §AIMS
    - project_alias_sources populated by the 7-rule construction
      per Annex E §AIMS.9
    - Return Provenance extracted per-instruction per Annex E §AIMS.9
      ReturnContract 4-tuple table

  Soundness property:
    borrow_sources type:

      borrow_sources : ArcVarId -> BorrowSource

      BorrowSource = <
        source: ArcVarId,
        path: List Int
      >

      Population invariant: every Project instruction creates exactly one
        borrow_sources entry; no other instruction creates entries;
        read-only after intraprocedural analysis.

      Source field traces through Let Var aliases via root(src) per
        Annex E §AIMS.9; path field is the FULL projection path
        from root (field-index list).

      Consumers per Annex E §AIMS.9:
        - DP-5: queries borrow_sources for active overlapping borrows
                + project_alias_sources for transitive live aliases
        - TF-14: projected variable locality widening propagates to
                borrow source

    project_alias_sources type:

      project_alias_sources : ArcVarId -> List ArcVarId

      Construction (precomputed once; 7 rules per Annex E §AIMS.9):
        R1: direct Project destinations -> Project root sources
            (tracing through Let Var aliases via root(src))
        R2: Let aliases (a = Let Var(b)) -> a maps to [b] union sources(b)
        R3: Jump-arg -> block-param transitive aliasing
        R4: CFG merge union sources from all predecessor Jump args
            tracing to different roots
        R5: Select aliases (dst = Select(cond, tA, fA)) ->
            dst maps to [tA, fA] union sources(tA) union sources(fA)
        R6: Transitive closure for nested Projects
        R7: Set / SetTag mutation tracking preserves prior aliases;
            no new alias entry created (in-place; no dst)

      Consumer: propagate_project_source_demand() per TF-14;
        invoked on every backward worklist iteration; widens
        src.cardinality (seq_add) + src.locality (max) per Annex E §AIMS.9 Consumer rule for BORROW entries (R1, R6 only).
        Non-borrow aliases (R2, R3, R5, R7) do NOT trigger
        propagate_project_source_demand(); they exist for DP-5 safety
        check only.

    Return Provenance per-instruction extraction table:

      Per Return value, trace structurally (NOT via AimsStateMap) through
      definitions; classify along 4 dimensions:
        <uniqueness: Uniqueness, preserves_freshness: Bool,
         locality: Locality, shape: Shape>

      Per Annex E §AIMS.9 (17-row table):
        Construct -> (u, true, bl, shape_from_ctor)
        Reuse -> (u, true, bl, inherited)
        CollectionReuse -> (u, true, bl, C)
        PartialApply -> (u, true, bl, Phi)
        Apply / Invoke (Unique contract) -> inherited
        Apply / Invoke (non-Unique contract) -> callee's contract values
        Apply / Invoke (no contract) -> (ms, false, top, Phi)
        ApplyIndirect / InvokeIndirect -> (ms, false, top, Phi)
        Project -> (ms, false, he, Phi)
        IsShared / Reset -> SCALAR (excluded)
        Let Literal / Let PrimOp -> SCALAR (excluded)
        Let Var(v) -> follow v
        Select <t, f> -> per-dim join with
                                                     scalar exclusion
        Parameter (or via Let chain) -> (ms, false, he, Phi)
        Unresolvable -> (ms, false, top, Phi)

      All return paths joined per IC-4:
        uniqueness(join), preserves_freshness(AND), locality(join), shape(join)

      Pre-widening escape state validation: downgrade Unique -> MaybeShared
        and preserves_freshness -> false when returned variable has
        escaping use BEFORE Return point per Annex E §AIMS.9
        Validation clause.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-04 (TF-14 + IA-5 step (1) alias-transfer proofs)
            + sec-05 (DP-5 alias-overlap proofs) + sec-06 (IC-4 return-contract
            extraction proofs)

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (per-rule construction R1-R7 + per-instruction extraction
                     17-row table)
      monotonicity (validates side-table widening preserves L-6 in
                    AimsStateMap consumers)
      lattice (validates project_alias_sources union + Return Provenance
               IC-4 join soundness)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-04 + sec-05 + sec-06 discharge side-table consumer proofs
